+	SETTING("experimental.noop_putllc_keeps_reservations", "Experimental", "FPS Experiments", "No-op PUTLLC keeps reservations", "With Accurate SPU Reservations on, an SPU atomic store that writes back unchanged data still succeeds only if the data and its reservation are unchanged, but no longer cancels the reservations other SPUs hold on the same data. SPUs that poll the same data then stop failing each other's atomic updates. Automatic enables it for Dragon Ball Z Budokai HD Collection and Call of Duty: Black Ops II; Black Ops II runs with Accurate SPU Reservations off, so there it changes nothing. Disabled cancels them as before. Takes effect on the next boot.", kind::RPCS3_IOS_SETTING_CHOICE, g_cfg.ios_experimental.noop_putllc_keeps_reservations, 0, 0, 0),
+	SETTING("experimental.rsx_idle_park", "Experimental", "FPS Experiments", "RSX idle park", "When the RSX command queue has stayed empty for one millisecond, the RSX thread sleeps in 50-microsecond steps instead of spinning, which frees a CPU core for the SPU and PPU threads. A memory flush, flip or ZCULL request from another thread wakes it at once; new guest commands are seen within one step. Applies with RSX FIFO Idle Wait set to Yield. Automatic enables it for every title; Disabled spins as before. Takes effect on the next boot.", kind::RPCS3_IOS_SETTING_CHOICE, g_cfg.ios_experimental.rsx_idle_park, 0, 0, 0),
+	SETTING("experimental.rsx_thread_priority", "Experimental", "FPS Experiments", "RSX thread priority", "Gives the RSX thread and the audio threads precedence over the PPU and SPU threads when the game asks for more CPU than the performance cores provide, as RPCS3 intends; iOS otherwise treats them alike. Automatic enables it for every title; Disabled gives every emulation thread the same priority as before. Takes effect on the next boot.", kind::RPCS3_IOS_SETTING_CHOICE, g_cfg.ios_experimental.rsx_thread_priority, 0, 0, 0),
+	SETTING("experimental.passive_lock_fairness", "Experimental", "FPS Experiments", "Passive lock fairness", "When a PPU or SPU thread has waited a long time to resume guest memory access while SPUs keep taking reservation write locks, new write locks briefly let it through first. No lock is skipped. Automatic enables it for every title; Disabled restores the previous lock order. Takes effect on the next boot.", kind::RPCS3_IOS_SETTING_CHOICE, g_cfg.ios_experimental.passive_lock_fairness, 0, 0, 0),
+	GAME_SETTING("experimental.metal_renderer", "Experimental", "Renderer", "Native Metal 4 renderer", "Draws the PlayStation 3 graphics with the native Metal 4 renderer instead of Vulkan on MoltenVK: textures, render-to-texture and readback, exact occlusion queries, MSAA and native overlays run on Metal 4; paths still missing are counted in the log. Needs iOS 26 and a Metal 4 GPU, otherwise Vulkan is used. Automatic keeps Vulkan. Takes effect on the next boot.", kind::RPCS3_IOS_SETTING_CHOICE, g_cfg.ios_experimental.metal_renderer, 0, 0, 0),
+	GAME_SETTING("experimental.ppu_grace", "Experimental", "FPS Experiments", "PPU grace after starvation", "When a PPU or SPU thread finally resumes guest memory access after starving behind SPU reservation write locks, new write locks wait about 100 us more before stopping the PPU threads again, so the thread runs before the next one. Every write lock is still taken and parks every PPU thread; it is only taken later, within the same bound. Automatic enables it for every title, with Passive lock fairness. Takes effect on the next boot.", kind::RPCS3_IOS_SETTING_CHOICE, g_cfg.ios_experimental.ppu_grace, 0, 0, 0),
+	SETTING("experimental.writer_yield_no_depress", "Experimental", "FPS Experiments", "Writer lock yield without depression", "When an SPU or PPU atomic write that holds the reservation write lock waits for other threads, it yields its CPU core without iOS lowering its priority for a whole scheduling quantum (about 10 ms), so the PPU threads it keeps waiting resume sooner. No lock is skipped. Automatic enables it for every title; Disabled yields as before. Takes effect on the next boot.", kind::RPCS3_IOS_SETTING_CHOICE, g_cfg.ios_experimental.writer_yield_no_depress, 0, 0, 0),
+	SETTING("experimental.put_epoch_horizon", "Experimental", "FPS Experiments", "Texture epoch at the PUT horizon", "With Texture Validation Per FIFO Batch, every new batch of guest commands the RSX noticed made every texture check its contents again, even while the RSX was still executing commands published earlier. The recheck now starts when the RSX reaches the first command that was not yet published at the previous one; semaphores, RSX writes and the end of a frame recheck as before. Every texture is still checked before any command published after its last check uses it. Automatic enables it for God of War III; Disabled rechecks at every batch noticed, as before. Takes effect on the next boot.", kind::RPCS3_IOS_SETTING_CHOICE, g_cfg.ios_experimental.put_epoch_horizon, 0, 0, 0),
+	SETTING("experimental.texture_prehash", "Experimental", "FPS Experiments", "Texture pre-validation", "With Texture Validation Per FIFO Batch, a texture used again after new guest commands is hashed again to check that the game did not change it. A worker thread now hashes, as soon as new commands arrive, the textures the previous frame checked next, so the RSX thread finds the result ready. Every byte is still checked and a result is used only for the commands it was taken for. Needs Texture Validation Per FIFO Batch. Automatic enables it for God of War III; Disabled hashes on the RSX thread as before. Takes effect on the next boot.", kind::RPCS3_IOS_SETTING_CHOICE, g_cfg.ios_experimental.texture_prehash, 0, 0, 0),
+	SETTING("experimental.texture_residency", "Experimental", "FPS Experiments", "Texture residency cap", "When cached textures use more than 768 MB, the textures no draw has used for 64 frames are released, at most 128 MB every 16 frames: first those whose memory the game has since filled with another texture, then the oldest. Textures in use are kept; a released texture the game samples again is uploaded again from its memory. Limits the memory held by textures whose memory the game has reused for other data. Automatic enables it for God of War III; Disabled keeps every texture until it is found stale. Takes effect on the next boot.", kind::RPCS3_IOS_SETTING_CHOICE, g_cfg.ios_experimental.texture_residency, 0, 0, 0),
+	SETTING("experimental.scoped_texture_revalidation", "Experimental", "FPS Experiments", "Scoped texture revalidation", "With texture validation per FIFO batch, a render target the RSX writes back to memory or commits over a range makes only the textures over that range check their contents again, instead of every texture. Guest commands, semaphores and the end of a frame still recheck every texture. Automatic enables it for God of War III, Call of Duty: Black Ops II, Bladestorm and Assassin's Creed; Disabled rechecks every texture after any RSX write as before. Takes effect on the next boot.", kind::RPCS3_IOS_SETTING_CHOICE, g_cfg.ios_experimental.scoped_texture_revalidation, 0, 0, 0),
